(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Background: Whether restricting eating to specific hours influences appetite hormones and) Tj
T*
(eating behavior patterns is not well established. Methods: 39 overweight/obese adults) Tj
T*
(\(mean age 59 years, BMI 35.4\) with prediabetes were randomized to 10-hour restricted) Tj
T*
(eating \(n=19\) or 16-hour conventional pattern \(n=20\) for 12 weeks with equal caloric) Tj
T*
(intake. Eating behaviors were assessed by questionnaire; fasting leptin, adiponectin,) Tj
T*
(C-reactive protein, cortisol, and postload ghrelin were measured. Results: Weight loss was) Tj
T*
(comparable between groups \(2.6% restricted vs 2.4% conventional\). Both arms showed) Tj
T*
(increased dietary restraint and decreased disinhibition and hunger sensation scores. No) Tj
T*
(significant between-group differences emerged for appetite hormones or inflammatory) Tj
T*
(markers despite mean reductions in leptin, adiponectin changes, and C-reactive protein.) Tj
T*
(Interpretation: Modest weight loss occurred in both conditions, with both groups) Tj
T*
(demonstrating improvements in eating behavior scores. However, significant differential) Tj
T*
(effects on appetite regulation or inflammation were not detected. Further investigation in) Tj
T*
(larger populations is needed.) Tj
